{"id":"0b163842f6e1db06","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-thm-forcing-completeness.md","title":"Closure Preservation of Inaccessibility","display":"thm-forcing-completeness — Closure Preservation of Inaccessibility","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-forcing-completeness","aliases":["58-thm-forcing-completeness"],"display":"thm-forcing-completeness — Closure Preservation of Inaccessibility","depends_on":["[[../batch06/58-df-proper.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-zfc-kappa-closed-poset.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-ctm.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-structure.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-assignment.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-forcing-completeness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-forcing-completeness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-forcing-completeness — Closure Preservation of Inaccessibility"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"8935dcac821c0104\" href=\"?note=8935dcac821c0104\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-proper.md\">../batch06/58-df-proper.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f6ffd36213690e39\" href=\"?note=f6ffd36213690e39\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-zfc-kappa-closed-poset.md\">../batch04/58-df-zfc-kappa-closed-poset.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"06ee5d7ff126e916\" href=\"?note=06ee5d7ff126e916\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md\">../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"46b2495f214783c3\" href=\"?note=46b2495f214783c3\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md\">../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-ctm.md\">../batch06/58-df-ctm.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-structure.md\">../batch18/58-df-structure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-assignment.md\">../batch03/58-df-assignment.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\\in V\">\\(M\\in V\\)</span> (the carrier of a countable transitive membership model), <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_{\\in}\">\\(\\mathcal L_{\\in}\\)</span> (its explicit language), and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ZFC}_{\\mathcal L_{\\in}}\">\\(\\operatorname{ZFC}_{\\mathcal L_{\\in}}\\)</span> (the theory code)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P,\\leq_P,1_P,\\kappa\\in M\">\\(P,\\leq_P,1_P,\\kappa\\in M\\)</span> (forcing and cardinal parameters)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\psi_{\\mathrm{cl,inacc}}(v_0,v_1,v_2,v_3)\">\\(\\psi_{\\mathrm{cl,inacc}}(v_0,v_1,v_2,v_3)\\)</span> (a fixed formula code saying that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(v_0,v_1,v_2)\">\\((v_0,v_1,v_2)\\)</span> is a <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"&lt;v_3\">\\(&lt;v_3\\)</span>-closed forcing poset and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_3\">\\(v_3\\)</span> is strongly inaccessible)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_{\\mathrm{inacc}}(v_0)\">\\(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{inacc}}(v_0)\\)</span> (a fixed formula code defining strong inaccessibility)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTMInLanguage}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CTMInLanguage}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ForcingRelation}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ForcingRelation}_S\\)</span> (predicates and projections from the dependencies)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\check\\kappa^P\">\\(\\check\\kappa^P\\)</span> (the canonical <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>-name for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S\\)</span> 使用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"8935dcac821c0104\" href=\"?note=8935dcac821c0104\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-proper.md\">../batch06/58-df-proper.md</a>；赋值函数的定义域为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Var}_S=\\{v_i:i\\in\\omega\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Var}_S=\\{v_i:i\\in\\omega\\}\\)</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CTMInLanguage}_S\n(M,\\mathcal L_{\\in},\\operatorname{ZFC}_{\\mathcal L_{\\in}})\n\\land P,\\leq_P,1_P,\\kappa\\in M\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\psi_{\\mathrm{cl,inacc}},\\varphi_{\\mathrm{inacc}}\n\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_{\\in})\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\exists\\mathcal M,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathcal M,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\n(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal L_{\\in},\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{31mm}\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\n\\land s(v_0)=P\\land s(v_1)=\\leq_P\\land s(v_2)=1_P\\land s(v_3)=\\kappa\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{31mm}\\land\\operatorname{Sat}(\\psi_{\\mathrm{cl,inacc}},s)\n\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\mathrm{ForcingRelation}_S\n\\bigl(M,1_P,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{inacc}},\n\\langle\\check\\kappa^P\\rangle,P,\\leq_P\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CTMInLanguage}_S\n(M,\\mathcal L_{\\in},\\operatorname{ZFC}_{\\mathcal L_{\\in}})\n\\land P,\\leq_P,1_P,\\kappa\\in M\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\psi_{\\mathrm{cl,inacc}},\\varphi_{\\mathrm{inacc}}\n\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_{\\in})\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\exists\\mathcal M,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathcal M,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\n(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal L_{\\in},\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{31mm}\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\n\\land s(v_0)=P\\land s(v_1)=\\leq_P\\land s(v_2)=1_P\\land s(v_3)=\\kappa\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{31mm}\\land\\operatorname{Sat}(\\psi_{\\mathrm{cl,inacc}},s)\n\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\mathrm{ForcingRelation}_S\n\\bigl(M,1_P,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{inacc}},\n\\langle\\check\\kappa^P\\rangle,P,\\leq_P\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Internal truth is evaluated by a selected satisfaction recursion and assignment; the former shorthand <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\\models\\ulcorner\\cdots\\urcorner\">\\(M\\models\\ulcorner\\cdots\\urcorner\\)</span> left both objects implicit.</li>\n<li>The conclusion uses the canonical six-place forcing relation, including the ground model, condition, one-variable formula code, one-name tuple, forcing carrier, and order.</li>\n<li>A <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"&lt;\\kappa\">\\(&lt;\\kappa\\)</span>-closed forcing adds no sequences of ordinals of length below <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>, so it preserves the regularity and strong-limit facts witnessing strong inaccessibility.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch06/58-df-proper.md","status":"resolved","id":"8935dcac821c0104","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-proper.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-zfc-kappa-closed-poset.md","status":"resolved","id":"f6ffd36213690e39","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-zfc-kappa-closed-poset.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md","status":"resolved","id":"06ee5d7ff126e916","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md","status":"resolved","id":"46b2495f214783c3","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch06/58-df-ctm.md","status":"resolved","id":"66d43bb76d055059","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-ctm.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad7